# Target C-II — two-leaf outer energy excludes the full-core branch through `t<=1.84365`

**Date:** 2026-09-15  
**Status:** proof-only full-core Type-II exclusion  
**Scope:** full-core/no-macroscopic-container Type-II branch  
**Dependencies:** scope-safe `g=0.007707` residual stability; hostile-audited two-leaf outer-energy architecture; `t<=1.844` phasewise retained-outer-mass theorem; branch-aware physical center/leaf pair theorem; hostile-audited cross-phase endpoint-energy theorem  
**Certificate:** `research/verify_target_c_two_leaf_outer_energy_exclusion_t184365.py`  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** `STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.`

The two-leaf outer-energy argument can be propagated one more rounded step beyond the certified `1.84364` endpoint. The exact certificate proves

\[
\boxed{
\liminf_{D\to\infty}{q-k\over D}\ge1.84365
}
\]

at the present proof-only full-core scope.

This is close to the numerical ceiling of the current rounded propagation. The final contradiction margin is only about `1.2e-5 D`, so the proof uses explicit outward arithmetic at every load-bearing step.

The rounded package is

\[
h<0.000378,
\qquad
W<1.912711,
\qquad
E_{dom}>0.90689962,
\]

\[
z>2.21934,
\qquad
z_C,z_U,z_V>0.702,
\]

\[
U,V<0.5304.
\]

Thus each leaf carries more than `0.1716D` retained O-O pair weight. After discarding all pair weight with center degree at most half, each leaf still has more than `0.1349D` good O-O weight. The common-center/triangle-free argument then forces more selected outer directional energy than the total detour budget allows.

---

## 1. Residual stability remains in scope

Let

\[
C_{707}=2\sqrt{\Delta_2}+0.007707,
\qquad
\Delta_2={\pi\over2\sqrt3},
\]

and use

\[
t={q-k\over D},
\qquad
x={\kappa\over2},
\qquad
h=U_{net}-C_{707},
\qquad
c=1.05.
\]

The `g=.007707` residual-stability theorem is stated for `U_net<=2.013`. The older `t<=1.844` phase theorem gives

\[
z_C,z_U,z_V>0.616-o(1),
\]

hence total retained dominant outer-occurrence mass above `1.848D`. Therefore

\[
\delta\ge F(1.848)-o(1),
\qquad
F(s)=s-6\sin(s/6),
\]

and the exact certificate gives `F(1.848)>0.029`. At `t<=1.84365`,

\[
U_{net}
\le {9t\over2}-2\pi-2\delta
<1.956<2.013.
\]

Thus the residual estimate is valid without extending its scope:

\[
R:=U_{net}-W\le1.05h,
\tag{E65.1}
\]

where `W=C+U+V` is the dominant exact `pi/3` orbit mass.

