on the energy-feasible side.

Assume `z<=Z=2.21934`. The capped left side is increasing in `z`; the verifier gives derivative above `0.96`. On `delta>=F(Z)`, the adverse `x` motion reaches `delta=F(Z)`. At `h=H`, the boundary still has

